          "distinct": false,
          "id": "76a9cc32e609ec5a7466d487bc95119aaa97037f",
          "message": "test(site): deterministic visual-regression baselines — container-pinned, masked, advisory (sq-ymr2e.10) [FABLE-5] (#1492)\n\n* test(site): deterministic visual-regression baselines — WIP container-pinned lane + masks (sq-ymr2e.10) [FABLE-5]\n\nPreserved after session-limit kill; completion pass adds determinism/sensitivity evidence + PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(site): visual rig — open the palette via Control+K at the mobile viewport (sq-ymr2e.10) [FABLE-5]\n\nThe header CommandPaletteTrigger is `hidden lg:inline-flex` (app-shell.tsx), so at the\n390x844 visual-mobile viewport the role-based click could never resolve; the global\nControl+K binding (registered before the app-ready barrier) is the only open path there.\nDesktop keeps the deterministic trigger click. Verified in the pinned container: two\nconsecutive full-baseline regenerations byte-identical (sha256, 11/11), both matching the\ncommitted baselines; comparison mode 11 passed / 1 skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
